  SPlusVrs=4.06.00
  CrossCplrVrs=1.3
[END]
[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=The primary purpose of the File Reader module (comprising the SIMPL+||1
  Cmn2=module and its paired SIMPL# library) is to\\provide a thread-safe||1
  Cmn3=interface for reading and writing up to 256 digital, analog, and||1
  Cmn4=serial signals to and from files\\on a Crestron processor, supporting||1
  Cmn5=Text, CSV, XML, JSON, INI, and Binary formats. This enables persistent||1
  Cmn6=storage and\\retrieval of system states, configurations, or data||1
  Cmn7=in Crestron control systems, with auto-detection of formats during\\
  Cmn8=reads, error feedback, and mutex protection for concurrent operations.
  Cmn9=\\\\Optionally supports AES encryption of file contents.\\\\- INPUTS,||1
  Cmn10=OUTPUTS, PARAMETERS --------------------------------------------
  Cmn11=-----------------\\\\Parameters:\\- Format (Integer): Specifies||1
  Cmn12=the file format for write operations. Options: 1 (Text), 2 (CSV),||1
  Cmn13=3 (XML), 4 (JSON),\\    5 (INI), 6 (Binary).\\  Default: 4 (JSON).
  Cmn14=||1Used only for writes; reads auto-detect the format.\\- File_Location||1
  Cmn15=(String): The path to the file (e.g., "\\NVRAM\\"). Ensure the path||1
  Cmn16=is valid on the Crestron processor\\    (e.g., NVRAM or CF0). Required||1
  Cmn17=for both read and write.\\- Filename (String): The name of the file||1
  Cmn18=(e.g., "datafile"). Required for both read and write.\\- Default_Settle_Time||1
  Cmn19=(Time): After Set_Default_Values pulses (auto-create), wait this||1
  Cmn20=long before Write so external\\    logic can drive Digital/Analog/Serial||1
  Cmn21=inputs. Default 0.25s. DELAY units match SIMPL+ (0.01s ticks).\\
  Cmn22=\\Inputs:\\- Read (Digital): Pulse high to trigger a read operation||1
  Cmn23=from the file specified in Filename. Loads data into the\\  output||1
  Cmn24=signals if successful.\\- Write (Digital): Pulse high to trigger||1
  Cmn25=a write operation to the file specified in Filename, using the format||1
  Cmn26=from\\  the Format parameter. Saves data from the input signals.
  Cmn27=||1On success, copies all inputs to the corresponding\\  outputs (so||1
  Cmn28=the module state matches what was just written without requiring||1
  Cmn29=a Read).\\- Delete (Digital): Pulse high to delete the file specified||1
  Cmn30=in Filename. Updates File_Exists_FB and Feedback on\\    completion.
  Cmn31=\\- Delete_Backup (Digital): Pulse high to delete the backup file||1
  Cmn32=(*.bak) if it exists. Updates Backup_Exists_FB and\\    Feedback||1
  Cmn33=on completion.\\- Enable_Backup (Digital): When high, enables automatic||1
  Cmn34=backup (.bak) on writes.\\- Enable_Backup_History (Digital): When||1
  Cmn35=high, enables archiving of previous backups to dated .gz files during||1
  Cmn36=write\\    operations with backup enabled. If low, overwrites the||1
  Cmn37=.bak without archiving.\\- Restore_Backup (Digital): Pulse high||1
  Cmn38=to restore from .bak to Filename, if .bak exists.\\- Encrypt (Digital):
  Cmn39=||1When high, enables AES encryption on writes (using Encryption_Key).
  Cmn40=\\- Enable_Auto_Create (Digital): When high, manages the config||1
  Cmn41=file at startup / path change:\\    * File missing → pulse Set_Default_Values,||1
  Cmn42=wait Default_Settle_Time, Write (then I→O on success).\\    *||1
  Cmn43=File exists → automatic Read onto Digital/Analog/Serial outputs||1
  Cmn44=(program restart / path change restore).\\    Does not overwrite||1
  Cmn45=an existing file on create. One auto action per effective path until||1
  Cmn46=the path changes.\\- Format_Override (Analog): Overrides the Format||1
  Cmn47=parameter at runtime if value is 1-6; otherwise, uses the parameter.
  Cmn48=\\- Filename_Override (String): Overrides the Filename parameter||1
  Cmn49=at runtime if non-empty; otherwise, uses the parameter.\\- Digital_Input_[1-
  Cmn50=64] (Digital): Digital input values (0 or 1) to be written to the||1
  Cmn51=file. Ignored during read\\  operations. During auto-create, external||1
  Cmn52=logic should drive these after Set_Default_Values.\\- Analog_Input_[1-
  Cmn53=64] (Analog): Analog input values (0-65535) to be written to the||1
  Cmn54=file. Ignored during read\\  operations.\\- Serial_Input_[1-64]||1
  Cmn55=(String): Serial input strings (up to 256 characters each) to be||1
  Cmn56=written to the file. Ignored\\  during read operations.\\- Encryption_Key||1
  Cmn57=(String): The encryption key (e.g., a 16-character string for AES-
  Cmn58=128). Required if Encrypt is high.\\\\Outputs:\\- Detected_Format||1
  Cmn59=(Analog): After a read operation, indicates the auto-detected file||1
  Cmn60=format: 1 (Text), 2 (CSV),\\  3 (XML), 4 (JSON), 5 (INI), 6 (Binary),||1
  Cmn61=or -1 (Error or undetected), -2 (Integrity check failed). Remains||1
  Cmn62=unchanged\\  after writes. JSON: optional crc32 is not a hard integrity||1
  Cmn63=reject.\\- Feedback (String): Provides status or error messages||1
  Cmn64=after read/write operations (e.g., "Valid JSON detected and\\  parsed"||1
  Cmn65=or "Error: File not found"). Useful for debugging or display on||1
  Cmn66=touchpanels.\\- File_Exists_FB (Digital): High (1) if the file at||1
  Cmn67=Filename exists, low (0) otherwise. Updated on module\\  initialization||1
  Cmn68=and whenever Filename_Override changes (if dynamically connected).
  Cmn69=\\- File_Not_Exist_FB (Digital): High (1) if the file at Filename||1
  Cmn70=does not exist, low (0) otherwise. Updated on module\\  initialization||1
  Cmn71=and whenever Filename_Override changes (if dynamically connected).
  Cmn72=\\- File_Busy_FB (Digital): High (1) while a file operation (read,||1
  Cmn73=write, delete, auto-create) is in progress, low (0)\\  otherwise.
  Cmn74=\\- File_Encrypted_FB (Digital): High (1) if the file appears to||1
  Cmn75=be encrypted (based on header), low (0) otherwise.\\- Backup_Exists_FB||1
  Cmn76=(Digital): High (1) if the backup file at Filename.bak exists, low||1
  Cmn77=(0) otherwise. Updated on module\\  initialization and after operations.
  Cmn78=\\- Set_Default_Values (Digital): 1 ms pulse when auto-create needs||1
  Cmn79=defaults applied to the module inputs. Wire this to\\  your SIMPL||1
  Cmn80=logic that drives Digital/Analog/Serial inputs with default configuration||1
  Cmn81=values.\\- File_Size (String): The formatted size of the file (e.
  Cmn82=g., "1.23 KB" or "456 bytes" or "7.89 MB"). Updated after\\    reads||1
  Cmn83=or on init/Filename_Override change.\\- Digital_Output_[1-64] (Digital):
  Cmn84=||1Digital values (0 or 1) loaded from the file after a successful||1
  Cmn85=read, or copied\\  from Digital_Input_[1-64] after a successful||1
  Cmn86=write. Unchanged on error.\\- Analog_Output_[1-64] (Analog): Analog||1
  Cmn87=values (0-65535) loaded from the file after a successful read, or||1
  Cmn88=copied\\  from Analog_Input_[1-64] after a successful write. Unchanged||1
  Cmn89=on error.\\- Serial_Output_[1-64] (String): Serial strings loaded||1
  Cmn90=from the file after a successful read, or copied from\\  Serial_Input_[1-
  Cmn91=64] after a successful write. Unchanged on error.\\\\Usage Instructions:
  Cmn92=\\- Connect Read/Write/Delete/Delete_Backup/Restore_Backup to digital||1
  Cmn93=triggers (e.g., buttons or logic).\\- For writes: Set input signals,||1
  Cmn94=select Format, specify File_Location and Filename (or Filename_Override),||1
  Cmn95=set\\    Enable_Backup if desired, then pulse Write. On success,||1
  Cmn96=outputs mirror the inputs that were written.\\- For reads: Specify||1
  Cmn97=File_Location and Filename (or Filename_Override), pulse Read; check||1
  Cmn98=Detected_Format and Feedback\\    for results, then use output signals.
  Cmn99=\\- For deletes: Specify File_Location and Filename (or Filename_Override),||1
  Cmn100=pulse Delete; check Feedback and\\    File_Exists_FB for results.
  Cmn101=\\- For backup deletes: Specify File_Location and Filename (or Filename_Override)
  Cmn102=, pulse Delete_Backup; check Feedback and\\    Backup_Exists_FB||1
  Cmn103=for results.\\- For restore: Specify File_Location and Filename||1
  Cmn104=(or Filename_Override), pulse Restore_Backup; check Feedback.\\-
  Cmn105=||1For encryption: Set Encrypt high and provide Encryption_Key for||1
  Cmn106=writes. For reads, encryption is auto-detected via\\    header;||1
  Cmn107=provide the correct key if File_Encrypted_FB is high.\\- For auto||1
  Cmn108=config (replace external Not_Exist → defaults → Write, and Exist||1
  Cmn109=→ Read on restart):\\    1. Hold Enable_Auto_Create high.\\||3
  Cmn110=||12. Wire Set_Default_Values to logic that asserts default values||1
  Cmn111=on Digital/Analog/Serial inputs.\\    3. On init (or path change):
  Cmn112=\\         - File missing → Set_Default_Values → settle →||1
  Cmn113=Write → outputs mirror inputs.\\         - File exists → Read||1
  Cmn114=→ outputs load from file (restart restore).\\    4. Existing files||1
  Cmn115=are never overwritten by auto-create. One auto action per effective||1
  Cmn116=path (retry after path change).\\- Backups are created as [FileName].
  Cmn117=[FileExtension].bak in the same directory. If Enable_Backup_History||1
  Cmn118=is high, old\\    backups are archived to .bak.yyyyMMdd.gz.\\- Use||1
  Cmn119=Format_Override (1-6) to override the Format parameter at runtime.
  Cmn120=\\- Use Filename_Override (non-empty string) to override the Filename||1
  Cmn121=parameter at runtime.\\- Thread-safe via mutex; multiple instances||1
  Cmn122=can share files but operations are serialized.\\- Errors are reported||1
  Cmn123=via Feedback and Crestron console (GenerateUserError).\\- Supports||1
  Cmn124=up to 64 signals per type (expandable to 256); unused signals are||1
  Cmn125=ignored if zero/empty.\\- Ensure the paired SIMPL# DLL (File Reader.
  Cmn126=dll) is deployed and referenced correctly.\\- JSON reads accept||1
  Cmn127=industry-standard objects with digitals / analogs / serials arrays||1
  Cmn128=(case-insensitive\\  names, optional nested data/signalData, optional||1
  Cmn129=crc32, shorter arrays, boolean digitals). crc32 is\\  never required||1
  Cmn130=for a successful JSON read.\\- 4-Series focused packaging.\\\\-||1
  Cmn131=VERSION HISTORY ------------------------------------------------
  Cmn132=------------------\\\\v3.0  8/4/2025  Generated by AI at the instruction||1
  Cmn133=of RGW\\- Wanted to add JSON files to the mix\\    8/5/2025  Modified||1
  Cmn134=by AI at the request of RGW\\- Added File_Exists_FB feedback\\-||1
  Cmn135=Added Delete functionality\\- Added File_Busy_FB feedback\\- Added||1
  Cmn136=File_Size and integrity checks\\- Added CSV and INI formats; updated||1
  Cmn137=format order\\- Added Backup/Rollback functionality\\- Changed File_Size||1
  Cmn138=to serial output with formatted size (bytes/KB/MB)\\- Added optional||1
  Cmn139=encryption support (AES) with Encrypt enable and Encryption_Key\\
  Cmn140=- Added File_Encrypted_FB feedback to indicate if the file on disk||1
  Cmn141=is encrypted (via header detection)\\- Added Backup_Exists_FB feedback||1
  Cmn142=to indicate if the backup file exists\\    8/6/2025  Modified by||1
  Cmn143=AI at the request of RGW\\- Added optional backup history with Enable_Backup_Hist
  Cmn144=ory input\\- Added Format_Override analog input to override Format||1
  Cmn145=parameter at runtime\\- Added Filename_Override string input to||1
  Cmn146=override Filename parameter at runtime\\- Added Delete_Backup digital||1
  Cmn147=input to delete the .bak file\\- Made Format parameter and override||1
  Cmn148=1-based (1=Text to 6=Binary)\\    8/6/2025  Modified by RGW\\- Requirements||1
  Cmn149=for File_Location and FilePath_Overrifde$ have changed; the filename||1
  Cmn150=and file extension has been\\    removed\\- Removed FilePath_Override$||1
  Cmn151=serial input\\- Added Filename parameter and Filename_Override serial||1
  Cmn152=input\\- Requirements for Filename and Filename_Override have changed;||1
  Cmn153=the file extension is now omitted from the name\\- File Extensions||1
  Cmn154=are now automatically appended to the Filename and Filename_Override,||1
  Cmn155=based on the value of Format\\    and/or Format_Override\\\\v3.1||1
  Cmn156=||12/25/2026  RGW\\- Added File_Not_Exist_FB, which is actual, rather||1
  Cmn157=than derivative\\\\v3.1.1  5/1/2026  RGW\\- Corrected text detection||1
  Cmn158=in the Read() block causing signals to sometimes not be read\\-||1
  Cmn159=Removed parameter formatting from the Simpl+ code in preparation||1
  Cmn160=for packaging inside a Simpl module wrapper\\\\v3.1.2  7/16/2026||1
  Cmn161=||1RGW / AI\\- Fixed Digital_Output_[x] not asserting after a successful||1
  Cmn162=read (explicit 0/1 digital assignment from\\  Simpl# ushort values)\\
  Cmn163=- JSON read now accepts industry-standard JSON: optional crc32 (no||1
  Cmn164=hard integrity reject), case-insensitive\\  property names, optional||1
  Cmn165=data/signalData wrappers, short arrays, boolean/numeric digital||1
  Cmn166=elements\\- Paired Simpl# source: FileReader20260623.cs (rebuild||1
  Cmn167=File Reader.clz / .dll after updating)\\\\v3.2.0  7/16/2026  RGW||1
  Cmn168=/ AI\\- On successful Write, copy Digital/Analog/Serial inputs to||1
  Cmn169=the corresponding outputs (explicit 0/1 for digitals)\\- Auto-create||1
  Cmn170=when file is missing and Enable_Auto_Create is high:\\    pulse||1
  Cmn171=Set_Default_Values → wait Default_Settle_Time → Write (then||1
  Cmn172=I→O copy on success)\\- Does not overwrite existing files; one||1
  Cmn173=auto-create attempt per effective path until path changes\\- Intended||1
  Cmn174=to replace external Not_Exist_FB → load defaults → Write routines||1
  Cmn175=in SIMPL\\\\v3.2.1  7/16/2026  RGW / AI\\- Enable_Auto_Create now||1
  Cmn176=also auto-Reads when the file already exists (startup / path change||1
  Cmn177=restore).\\  Previously only UpdateFileExists ran on restart (Exists_FB||1
  Cmn178=+ size) with no Read onto outputs.\\
[END]
